From: iOSPlus10 display agent (dpu)
Subject: [PATCH] negroni fb: panel double buffering with a DPU base flip (0269)

The UEFI auto-refresh scans one buffer (the panel memory 0xb8000000) on every TE, and the
GPU 2D copy (0231/0267) or the CPU copy writes that same buffer at a phase the scan does
not know: tearing, and a CPU copy can race a GPU copy still in flight (README-gpu-kernel.md
section 18; audit docs/audit/2026-10-26-display.md 2.1 and 3.1).

negronifb_dbuf=1 (default 0): three panel buffers (negronifb_dbufn=2|3): the panel memory
and two more after it in the splash region (0xb89f0000, 0xb93e0000, 0x9f0000 each). A
one-layer full-panel frame goes into a free buffer; when its copy is done (GPU fence, or at
once for the CPU) the pipes get its address: SSPP_SRC0_ADDR of the pipe(s) the 0234 probe
found fetching the panel memory + CTL_FLUSH (pipe bits + CTL bit 17) of the CTL driving
INTF_1 (sde_hw_sspp.c:925-948, sde_hw_ctl.c:685-711, sspp_tbl :78-79). The engine takes
the flush at the next auto-refresh frame start, so a whole frame shows, never half a copy.
The buffer shown before is free once CTL_FLUSH reads back clear. Other frames (several
layers, part of the panel) wait until nothing is outstanding and are drawn into the shown
buffer (single-buffer way). Two buffers would cap the GPU path at 60 frames/s (flip one
tick after the copy, the old buffer free one tick after the flip).

- vsyncFired: dbufTick at the tick start and end (latch, flip the newest finished copy;
  not while presentFinish or a 0256 shift still draws into it), dbufTarget before a frame
  is taken (no free buffer: the frame stays pending, "waits"), dbufQueued after present().
- Display off: zeroCopyStop(true) parks (the 0275 black goes into the shown buffer, no
  flip). Panic: the pipes go back to the panel memory (zeroCopyRestore) for the panic text.
- A flip not taken in 1 s (not counted while the display is off or the 0268 wake has the
  auto-refresh paused): double buffering off for the boot, pipes back on the panel memory.
- NegroniGPU.cpp: one GPU mapping per panel buffer (4), kept; before, a new panelPhys
  unmapped the old one while a copy into it could still be queued.
- 0234's slots (zeroCopyInit slotSize) and its display-surface bound now end at NEGRONI_DB_END
  (the splash end - 16 KiB): never into the 0268 DSI command buffer.
- Off with zero-copy (0234 has the same splash space), without the 0234 probe
  (negronifb_dpuprobe=0) or with an unexpected pipe layout.
Logs: "NEGRONI FB: 0269 double buffering on: 3 panel buffers ...", the first 4 flips
"NEGRONI FB: 0269 flip N: buffer B at 0x... (fence F), taken after N us", per second
"NEGRONI FB DBUF: flips/s N waits N in-place N latch max us N (...)".

